---
title: Configuring High Availability for Kubernetes Control Planes
---

The High availability feature must be configured during the cluster creation process. 

# Creating a Managed Kubernetes cluster

1. Log into the **Nebius AI Cloud Console**.
2. Navigate to the cluster creation wizard. 
**Create Managed Kubernetes Cluster** page opens. 
3. Enter a cluster **Name** (e.g., `blue-roundworm-cluster-2`) 
4. In **Labels**, add identifiers.
4. Configure your **Control plane**.

**To enable HA feature:**

a. Check the **High availability** switch is enabled by default (it is enabled by default). 

b. Select your desired **Kubernetes version** (e.g., `1.33`) from the drop-down menu and establish whether you need to **Enable** a **Public endpoint** to securely access your cluster via the open internet.

**To disable HA feature:**

a. Check the **High availability** switch is enabled by default (it is enabled by default). If enabled, toggle the switch OFF.

5. In the **Network** section, select your destination infrastructure. You can select the pre-configured **`default-network`** and its matching **`default-subnet`**.
6. Review your configurations details and click **Create cluster**.

